Z||000000||SLYGUY||09-20-2001||02:41 AM|||| <P>I've had the brakes checked out because of an annoying click click when I let up on the brakes just before I come to a stop. Under medium or heavy braking it won't make this sound, only with gradual braking.<P>Folks at Midas couldn't find anything wrong with it. <P>Had to have the right front rotor replaced because the caliper froze solid and ground the pads into it till they were gone. First time I had ever seen this. What could of contaminated that caliper and made it lock up?<P>Brakes feel perfect (despite that click) and stops sure. Doesn't pull either way and pedal travel is good.<P>What gives  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"> <P>Sly<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Alex4mula||09-20-2001||08:43 AM||||My Formula is doing that too. Started with a low noise click and now is louder. In my case it is the caliper. The slider pins are worn and the caliper has some small play. When you break hard everything holds tight toguether (no click) but when applying small preasure it can move and thus the click. Very probable your case too. To me the solution is to replace the whole caliper. If you replace only the pins the caliper bore will still be worn out and give you the same problem again.||||reg||1
Z||000002||SLYGUY||09-20-2001||01:56 PM||||Thanks Alex. That's what I'll do.<P>Sly||||reg||1
